From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: François Roux <franzelfranzel@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:27:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] wifi: ath12k: skip hardware rfkill setup on Microsoft
 Surface devices
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backport the upstream Surface rfkill fix without code changes. Adjust
hunk line numbers for the pinned v7.3 tree.

On DT boots the Surface WCN7850 hardware rfkill input reports radio off.
ACPI can already disable the unusable input, but the DT boot cannot read
that policy. Match the upstream board and hardware revision table before
programming hardware rfkill. Software airplane mode remains available.

M8 on this Denali LCD reports WMI radio_state 1 (OFF), soft=0, hard=1.
Windows _DSM function 2 returns 0x60, with the rfkill bit clear.

Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/ath/ath.git/commit/?id=5949d1910f13c20f6ebcd26eec9e0c02cb4951aa
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261006062728.45007-1-franzelfranzel@gmail.com
Assisted-by: Codex gpt-6.1-sol
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
index 3ed98eb746b5be..c9df99bc54fdef 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -72,6 +72,35 @@ ath12k_mem_profile_based_param ath12k_mem_profile_based_param[] = {
 	},
 };
 
+/*
+ * On these machines the OS cannot control the WCN7850 hardware rfkill
+ * input, which reads as "radio off", so hardware rfkill must stay
+ * disabled. Ideally this would come from the connector node of the board
+ * DT, but that binding does not exist yet.
+ */
+static const struct ath12k_core_broken_rfkill_table {
+	enum ath12k_hw_rev hw_rev;
+	const char *compatible;
+} ath12k_core_broken_rfkill_table[] = {
+	{ ATH12K_HW_WCN7850_HW20, "microsoft,denali" },
+	{ ATH12K_HW_WCN7850_HW20, "microsoft,romulus13" },
+	{ ATH12K_HW_WCN7850_HW20, "microsoft,romulus15" },
+	{ /* Sentinel */ }
+};
+
+static bool ath12k_core_rfkill_is_broken(struct ath12k_base *ab)
+{
+	const struct ath12k_core_broken_rfkill_table *entry;
+
+	for (entry = ath12k_core_broken_rfkill_table; entry->compatible; entry++) {
+		if (ab->hw_rev == entry->hw_rev &&
+		    of_machine_is_compatible(entry->compatible))
+			return true;
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
 static int ath12k_core_rfkill_config(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct ath12k *ar;
@@ -83,6 +112,9 @@ static int ath12k_core_rfkill_config(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	if (ath12k_acpi_get_disable_rfkill(ab))
 		return 0;
 
+	if (ath12k_core_rfkill_is_broken(ab))
+		return 0;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++) {
 		ar = ab->pdevs[i].ar;
 
